<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yongle Encyclopedia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1403">1403</a>–<a href="/years/1408">1408</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Yongle Dadian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yongle Encyclopedia was a vast Chinese compendium commissioned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> and completed in 1408. More than 2,000 scholars compiled 22,877 chapters in over 11,000 volumes, copying earlier works on history, philosophy, literature, science and the arts. The original was lost, and less than 4 per cent of a 16th-century copy survives after losses in later wars, especially in 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yongle-encyclopedia.jpg" alt="Yongle Encyclopedia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LW Yang · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yongle_Encyclopedia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
